# Development Environment Variables Example
# Copy this file to .dev.vars and fill in your actual values
# NEVER commit .dev.vars to version control!

# =============================================================================
# ADMIN CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================

# Admin Session Secret
# A secure random string used to sign admin session cookies
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=your_admin_session_secret_here

# Encryption Key
# A 32-byte base64-encoded key used for encrypting sensitive data in the database
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
ENCRYPTION_KEY=your_base64_encoded_32_byte_encryption_key_here

# =============================================================================
# EMAIL CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================
#
# The Cloudflare Email Service binding (see wrangler.toml [[send_email]])
# is the zero-config default for sending. To override the default from
# address (otherwise the binding's own default is used), set:
#
# EMAIL_FROM=noreply@yourdomain.com
#
# Optional legacy SendGrid path (deprecated; remove in release 2):
# SENDGRID_API_KEY=your_sendgrid_api_key
# SENDGRID_FROM_EMAIL=noreply@yourdomain.com
# SENDGRID_TEMPLATE_CONFIRMATION=template_id
# SENDGRID_TEMPLATE_PASSWORD_RESET=template_id
# SENDGRID_TEMPLATE_WELCOME=template_id
#
# Optional cross-account Cloudflare REST sender (overrides the binding
# when configured as the default provider in the admin UI):
# CF_ACCOUNT_ID=your_cloudflare_account_id
# CF_API_TOKEN=your_cloudflare_api_token

# =============================================================================
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
# =============================================================================
#
# 1. Copy this file:
#    cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#
# 2. Generate secure secrets:
#    ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET: openssl rand -base64 32
#    ENCRYPTION_KEY: openssl rand -base64 32
#
# 3. For production deployment:
#    - DO NOT use .dev.vars in production
#    - Set secrets using: wrangler secret put SECRET_NAME
#    - Update production vars in wrangler.toml [env.production.vars]
#
# 4. Test locally:
#    npm run dev
#
